The exact verifier requires only Python >= 3.10 and the Python standard
library.  No package installation is needed.

To check the rational certificate:

    python3 scripts/verify_certificate.py

To run the smoke test:

    python3 -m unittest discover -s tests

Optional: floating-point LP search
----------------------------------

The file scripts/search_lp_certificate.py rebuilds the floating-point LP used
to search for the certificate.  This is not part of the formal proof.  It
requires scipy:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate
    python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
    python3 -m pip install ".[search]"
    python3 scripts/search_lp_certificate.py

The proof-relevant artifact is scripts/verify_certificate.py, which checks the
final rationalized certificate exactly over Q.

Companion Max-2SAT appendix code
--------------------------------

The repository also contains three Max-2SAT scripts for the appendix-facing
`0.7425` construction line:

    scripts/max2sat_weighted_certificate_search.py
    scripts/max2sat_build_multirounding_curves.py
    scripts/max2sat_multi_rounding_certificate_search.py

These are floating-point LP construction scripts, not exact rational
verification code. They require NumPy and SciPy:

    python3 -m venv .venv
    source .venv/bin/activate
    python3 -m pip install --upgrade pip
    python3 -m pip install numpy scipy

The intended chain is:

1. use `max2sat_weighted_certificate_search.py` to produce a nonuniform base
   curve;
2. use `max2sat_build_multirounding_curves.py` to generate the nine scaled
   rounding curves;
3. use `max2sat_multi_rounding_certificate_search.py` to certify the
   multi-rounding witness.
